bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_any_match_bare_some_arm_takes_user_enum_unit_variant_2026-11-27, 0, "Repro (seed org2 4b4a35da446ffb70 = origin aa3d2f9e1f9, release/1.0.0, aarch64, JIT; interpreter correct): enum Opt: Some(i64) | Nope; fn g(x) -> i64: match x: Some(v): v / Nope: -5; g(Opt.Nope) returns 3 on the JIT (takes the Some arm and binds the nil word), -5 in the interpreter. The bare Some arm over an untyped subject tests Option presence, not the user enum variant. Found while fixing parse_family_strips_option_jit_native_2026-08-02."

