bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_any_match_bare_some_arm_takes_user_enum_unit_variant_2026-11-27, 4, "2026-11-27 Fable 3rd review: suspected native failure for a local user enum Option (bare id 1 never re-pointed while qualify stamps pkg.owner.Option) does not reproduce: Option::Some(42) lowers through the builtin Some path (no EnumWith of the user enum; MIR dump after qualify_enum_runtime_names with local_globals {Option, Bi} shows only pkg.owner.Bi as a qualified ctor), so the value carries id 1 natively and rt_enum_check_variant(x, 1, d) holds. Pinned green by native_project test erased_some_arm_binds_user_option_and_generic_owner_after_qualification (427: user Option 42 + generic Bi<i64>.Some(7) with its check ids re-pointed) and JIT test jit_generic_some_owner_binds_payload_through_untyped_parameter. Suggested binder id<2 ? unwrap : rt_enum_payload not taken: tip interpreter binds a non-Some/None enum value whole (mx2: SCol::Red SCol::Blue(9)), which that binder would turn into its payload. Non-blocking, open: the arm guard costs one rt_enum_check_variant per None/Some-declaring enum for subjects with id >= 2 (about 50 such enums under src/lib + src/compiler); a None-only enum branch has no dedicated test; when qualification drops a remap (bare-name id collision) the binder falls back to the whole value."
    seed_jit_any_match_bare_some_arm_takes_user_enum_unit_variant_2026-11-27, 3, "2026-11-27 Fable re-review FIX-FIRST (native lane): bare rt_enum_id == / != <bare-name id> compares are not re-pointed by requalify_enum_check_variant_ids, so in native-project builds the guard was inert and Opt.Some(4) bound the enum object. Guard and binder now test identity only through rt_enum_check_variant (value's own rt_enum_discriminant under E's id; E's Some disc for the binder), behind one rt_enum_id read (< 2 skips; binder keeps the chain when a user Option shares id 1). user_option_shaped_enums is cached per type-registry size and exempts a builtin-shaped global Option. Red->green: native_project tests.rs erased_some_arm_user_enum_identity_survives_runtime_name_qualification (2500300449412011 -> 42). Seed dd58bec3fc468fc3: all probes match the interpreter (pu2 4 -5, was 4 3; xm S4 S12 S4 - W S4; user Option fixture 42/99/unmatched). Lib 5183 pass, only baseline failures. Perf 3 rounds (4e7 erased matches): no Some-owning enum 0.20/0.22/0.20s vs origin 0.24/0.20/0.20s; one declared 0.33/0.35/0.36s vs origin 0.19/0.21/0.21s (origin binds nil there). Known limit (c): on the JIT a user enum Option shares id 1 with the builtin, so its non-Some unit variants pass the arm guard; native qualification gives it its own id."
    seed_jit_any_match_bare_some_arm_takes_user_enum_unit_variant_2026-11-27, 2, "2026-11-27 rebased onto 32d6250863e (review fix). user_option_shaped_enums now exempts only the generic builtin Option (a user enum Option shares runtime id 1) and also reads global_enum_defs; the guard reads rt_enum_id once (LetIn) and skips compares for ids < 2. Seed b50367c811bf41fb: user Option fixture some_arm=42 none_arm=99 none_via_some=unmatched; two-module probe S4 S12 S4 - W S4 on both lanes; Rust test file 6/6. Integration subset (12 Option/enum/pattern test files): 46 pass, 2 fail (list_optional_accessors_jit u64_optional_bindings..., optional_aggregate_copy_jit untyped_hir_expression...) -- both fail identically on origin aa3d2f9e1f9. Perf 3 alternated rounds vs branch-1 seed e6c71f325bb533c2: no Some-owning enum 0.23/0.19/0.22 vs 0.24/0.23/0.22s; with one declared 0.40/0.38/0.39 vs 0.20/0.22/0.20s (branch 1 binds nil there)."
    seed_jit_any_match_bare_some_arm_takes_user_enum_unit_variant_2026-11-27, 1, "2026-11-27 opus-bugbatch fix (stacked on parse_family part 1 d617c257cc3). Interpreter rule pinned (interpreter_patterns.rs): bare Some(v) over a value matches nil=no, raw=bind value, Option=payload, enum declaring Some/None=only its Some variant, other enum=bind whole value. JIT now: optional_some_condition (expr/control.rs) ANDs, for an ANY subject, rt_enum_id != E or rt_enum_check_variant(E, Some disc) per user enum E declaring Some/None (user_option_shaped_enums); the binder (stmt_lowering.rs) reads rt_enum_payload for those E and rt_unwrap_or_self otherwise, replacing part 1's program-wide gate. Red->green: seed_jit_erased_option_some_pattern.rs user-enum test 37 -> 45, raw-with-Opt-declared test 1000105 -> 1012105. g(Opt.Nope) with only Some/None arms now exhausts on both lanes (interp semantic error, JIT exhaustion abort), was JIT 3. Perf: no Some-owning enum declared 0.20-0.22s unchanged; with one declared 4e7 erased matches 0.22s (wrong values) -> 0.46s (correct). Not done: a bare None arm over a user enum None variant still uses rt_is_none."

